*  Chips;
*  Cryptography;
*  Satellite imagery;
*  Nuclear technology;
*  High-end EDA (Electronic Design Automation);
*  Biosafety tools;
*  Cyber ​​offensive and defensive capabilities.
This marks the institutionalized beginning of the tiered system you once described—ranging from "Top Secret" and "Classified" to "Government," "Private/Restricted," and "Public" versions.

II. Fable and Mythos demonstrate that "model tiering" has already emerged.
Anthropic’s own product documentation reveals a structure that goes beyond a single-layer model.
It describes Fable 5 as a "Mythos-class" model released to the general public but subject to strict safety constraints; meanwhile, Mythos 5 is a more powerful and sensitive version based on the same underlying capabilities. Designed primarily for fields like cybersecurity, biology, and healthcare, it is accessible only to a select group of vetted partners.
